\f0\b \cf2 Esc
\f1\b0 \cf0   =  Cancels active tool and returns to plain cursor\

\f0\b \cf2 A
\f1\b0 \cf0   =  Activates the elbow tool\

\f0\b \cf2 D
\f1\b0 \cf0   =  Activates the opposite-facing elbow tool\

\f0\b \cf2 S
\f1\b0 \cf0   =  Activates the straight-section tool\

\f0\b \cf2 R
\f1\b0 \cf0   =  Rotate the current piece tool; holding Shift goes counterclockwise\

\f0\b \cf2 F
\f1\b0 \cf0   =  Flips the current piece tool mirror-fashion; holding Shift uses the y-axis\
	(Interconnects only; logic gates can't be rotated)\

\f0\b \cf2 E (held down)
\f1\b0 \cf0   =  Stores the currently active tool and switches to erase-on-click\
	 mode (dragging also works); stored tool is restored on key release\

\f0\b \cf2 W (held down)
\f1\b0 \cf0   =  Stores the currently active tool and switches to click-and-drag-\
	to-move mode; stored tool is restored on key release\

\f0\b \cf2 CLICK
\f1\b0 \cf0   =  Draws current gate or piece to the board; straight pieces may be \
	drawn multiply by holding the click and dragging\

\f0\b \cf2 Shift + CLICK
\f1\b0 \cf0   =  Starts a new text label on the circuit board. Type the text,\
	hit Enter, then the position of the text can be changed by mouse dragging\
\

\f0\b \cf2 Y 
\f1\b0 \cf0  =  Resets the editor and clears the board\

\f0\b \cf2 Tab
\f1\b0 \cf0   =  Highlights the textbox in the top-right corner for entering a filename\
	(clicking it also works); hit Enter or Esc to stop entering text\

\f0\b \cf2 L
\f1\b0 \cf0   =  Attempts to load the circuit named in the textbox from the folder\
	resources/saved/; not necessary to include the .txt extension\

\f0\b \cf2 J
\f1\b0 \cf0   =  Saves the current configuration of the circuit board to a file called [text\
	in the textbox].txt. File will be found in resources/saved/. NOTE! If you load\
	a previously completed circuit, make changes or clear the board, and then \
	hit J while the name of that previous circuit is still in the textbox, the old\
	circuit will be overwritten with the new board, even an empty one\
\
